# Benchmark archives, fetched by each benchmark's build_data.py and cached
# beside it. The JSON they are distilled into is committed instead: it is two
# orders of magnitude smaller, and it is what the runners actually read.
*.zip

# The sweep outputs ARE committed, under benchmarks/*/results/. They are what
# the site is generated from, so CI can build the pages without nuclear data,
# and they are the record of what a given yani version scored. Single-case
# run.py output is not: it carries a per-nuclide breakdown at every cooling
# step, which is large and is a debugging aid rather than a result.
benchmarks/*/results/*_*_*.json

# The built site.
site/

# The generated figures and pages of the site.
docs/benchmarks/figures/

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
